 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Lookup is $O(1)$ relative to the number of grids, but depends on the depth of the OpenVDB tree and the interpolation cost. Bounding box calculation is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of grids in the file.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Depends on the OpenVDB file size. The global cache `s_vdbGridPool` retains loaded files in memory, which can lead to high memory usage if many large files are loaded [S1, unofficial].
